WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.680
What if I told you that, mathematically speaking, there's absolutely no proof that you end and the chair you're sitting on right now begins?

00:08.940 --> 00:10.540
It sounds totally absurd, right?

00:10.680 --> 00:11.160
Totally.

00:11.540 --> 00:13.520
Like something out of a late night dorm room debate.

00:13.780 --> 00:14.600
Yeah, exactly.

00:15.140 --> 00:21.220
But for like the last decade, biologists and cognitive scientists really thought they had finally found it.

00:21.300 --> 00:28.140
You know, a flawless mathematical formula to prove the physical existence of an individual organism.

00:28.140 --> 00:40.460
Right. They wanted a way to draw a hard, undeniable line around a cell or a brain or a conscious mind to just definitively state this right here is the system.

00:40.840 --> 00:43.200
And all that over there is the outside world.

00:43.540 --> 00:46.880
And it was treated as this mathematical holy grail, wasn't it?

00:46.900 --> 00:49.580
A concept called the Markov blanket.

00:50.300 --> 00:54.800
Oh, absolutely. The Markov blanket was the buzzword. Everyone wanted one.

00:54.800 --> 01:01.040
Right. Well, today we are looking at a paper that proves they have basically been doing the math wrong.

01:01.360 --> 01:06.620
We're taking a deep dive into an incredibly dense, rigorous piece of independent research.

01:06.880 --> 01:12.100
It just came out this month, November 2026, by a researcher named Flyxion.

01:12.580 --> 01:13.940
Yeah. And the title is a mouthful.

01:14.240 --> 01:22.140
It's called Closure Conditions on the Description of Bounded Systems, Markov Blankets in Graphical Models, and Dynamical Systems.

01:22.140 --> 01:25.340
It is a massive reality check.

01:25.460 --> 01:25.560
Yeah.

01:25.920 --> 01:28.720
And I just want to welcome you, the listener, to this journey.

01:29.060 --> 01:32.300
We know you're someone who loves a genuine intellectual challenge.

01:32.420 --> 01:36.840
You're not here for, you know, surface-level buzzwords or pop science headlines.

01:37.120 --> 01:38.880
No. You want the actual mechanics, right?

01:38.920 --> 01:41.340
The real ideas shaping our understanding of reality.

01:41.500 --> 01:41.940
Exactly.

01:41.940 --> 01:54.920
So today our mission is to completely separate the hard mathematics of the Markov blanket from the heavy, honestly pretty messy biological assumptions that scientists have just layered on top of it.

01:55.420 --> 02:01.060
We are going to find out if calculus and probability can actually prove that you are an individual.

02:01.580 --> 02:04.980
Spoiler alert, it's a lot more complicated than the biologists hoped.

02:04.980 --> 02:06.020
So much more complicated.

02:06.840 --> 02:08.020
Okay, let's unpack this.

02:08.260 --> 02:16.040
Because to understand how the math kind of got hijacked, we first have to understand what a Markov blanket was actually built to do in the first place.

02:16.420 --> 02:20.720
Right, which means we need to rewind a bit back to 1988.

02:21.460 --> 02:25.500
Because this concept definitely did not originate in biology or physics for that matter.

02:25.900 --> 02:27.760
No, it was probabilistics, right?

02:28.040 --> 02:28.300
AI.

02:28.300 --> 02:29.260
Exactly.

02:30.040 --> 02:36.500
It started with Judea Pearl, who was just an absolute titan in the field of graphical models and causal inference.

02:37.280 --> 02:45.960
And when Pearl originally defined the Markov blanket, it was this incredibly modest, highly specific, and purely statistical concept.

02:46.220 --> 02:48.760
Okay, so let's lay out that original definition for everyone.

02:48.760 --> 02:59.260
In graphical models, a Markov blanket is defined as a set of variables that screens one variable from all others under a fixed joint probability distribution.

03:00.100 --> 03:02.460
And the shorthand in the paper, it looks like a bit of algebra.

03:02.800 --> 03:10.660
It's x sub i, then a double perpendicular symbol, then x sub r, a vertical bar, and x sub m.

03:10.920 --> 03:11.200
Right.

03:11.320 --> 03:16.480
So let's break down those letters so we can actually visualize what Judea Pearl was talking about.

03:16.480 --> 03:21.520
So the x sub i, that is the internal variable.

03:22.060 --> 03:24.580
That's the specific thing you're trying to measure or predict.

03:25.000 --> 03:25.860
Okay, the target variable.

03:26.100 --> 03:26.240
Yeah.

03:26.720 --> 03:31.020
Then x sub m represents the Markov blanket itself, the surrounding set of variables.

03:31.780 --> 03:39.060
And x sub r is the rest of the universe, literally every other variable that exists outside of your little system.

03:39.380 --> 03:39.720
Got it.

03:40.200 --> 03:43.160
And that double perpendicular symbol in the middle, what does that mean?

03:43.160 --> 03:46.320
That symbol just means is conditionally independent of.

03:46.720 --> 03:55.280
So the whole formula is basically stating that your internal variable is conditionally independent of the rest of the universe, given the exact state of the blanket.

03:55.280 --> 04:01.560
I want to ground this immediately because, you know, conditional independence can be a really slippery concept if you're not a statistician.

04:01.700 --> 04:02.080
It really can.

04:02.080 --> 04:10.560
So imagine you have this highly accurate digital indoor weather station mounted on your living room wall, and it's wired to a bunch of sensors just outside your window.

04:11.080 --> 04:13.100
Thermometers, barometers, wind gauges, whatever.

04:13.800 --> 04:14.880
Okay, yeah, I have the visual.

04:14.880 --> 04:21.360
So let's say your goal is to predict the exact temperature of the air inside your living room, right next to the glass of the window.

04:22.100 --> 04:25.780
The digital display on your weather station is your Markov blanket.

04:26.180 --> 04:27.140
Right, that's x sub m.

04:27.380 --> 04:27.740
Exactly.

04:28.260 --> 04:35.000
And the chaotic weather outside, the actual wind, the sun beating down, the snow, that's the outside world, x sub r.

04:35.000 --> 04:50.400
So the concept of conditional independence here means that if you're staring right at that digital dial and it says 72 degrees, literally opening your front door and stepping out into a blizzard tells you absolutely nothing new about what the dial is predicting for your indoor temperature.

04:50.860 --> 04:52.720
That is a brilliant illustration, yeah.

04:53.100 --> 04:55.980
The dial completely screens you from the physical outside world.

04:56.500 --> 05:00.480
Now, obviously, this doesn't mean the outside world has no physical effect on the inside.

05:00.800 --> 05:03.060
Right, a blizzard will eventually cool down the glass.

05:03.060 --> 05:11.580
Exactly. But statistically, all the information from the blizzard that is relevant to your indoor prediction is perfectly captured by the numbers on that dial.

05:12.240 --> 05:15.940
If you know the state of the dial, you just don't need to go measure the snow.

05:16.400 --> 05:18.260
The information is completely mediated.

05:18.620 --> 05:20.260
The blanket captures everything you need.

05:20.920 --> 05:26.580
Now, Flyxion's paper points out a few mathematical quirks about this original 1988 definition.

05:26.580 --> 05:33.100
And these quirks are fascinating because they hint at the massive problems that are going to pop up later in the biology stuff.

05:33.420 --> 05:38.880
Yes, the paper notes three critical facts about Perl's graphical definition that honestly often get completely ignored.

05:39.660 --> 05:43.020
The first one is a mathematical technicality, but it's super vital.

05:43.800 --> 05:47.740
Technically speaking, in any given system, every single variable has a Markov blanket.

05:48.200 --> 05:48.900
Wait, hold on.

05:49.040 --> 05:51.240
Every variable? That seems entirely useless.

05:51.240 --> 05:55.220
I mean, if every variable has one, it's not exactly a special property.

05:55.640 --> 06:03.420
It isn't special at all in its rawest form because mathematically you can simply define the blanket as the set of literally all other variables in the system.

06:03.620 --> 06:04.000
Oh, I see.

06:04.320 --> 06:04.540
Right.

06:04.800 --> 06:12.480
Right. If you know everything else in the universe, then you are naturally, conditionally independent of whatever is left because there is literally nothing left to know.

06:12.480 --> 06:18.160
So, simply claiming that a system has a Markov blanket is essentially a vacuous statement. It means nothing.

06:18.380 --> 06:19.340
It means absolutely nothing.

06:19.500 --> 06:19.660
Okay.

06:19.800 --> 06:24.040
The entire value of claiming a blanket exists lies in restricting its size.

06:24.260 --> 06:28.580
You want to find a minimal blanket, you know, one that is significantly smaller than the rest of the universe.

06:28.900 --> 06:29.760
That makes total sense.

06:29.940 --> 06:38.320
It's like a biologist saying, I have found the boundary of this single-celled organism and the boundary is the entire Milky Way galaxy.

06:38.320 --> 06:41.380
Like, sure, but it doesn't help you isolate the cell.

06:41.380 --> 06:51.500
Precisely. Now, the second fact concerns uniqueness. When your probability distribution has a strictly positive density, the Markov boundary is unique.

06:51.640 --> 06:52.640
Let me stop you right there.

06:52.740 --> 06:52.900
Right.

06:53.840 --> 06:59.740
Strictly positive density. We really can't let that slide by. What does that actually mean in practice for a system?

07:00.000 --> 07:08.920
Fair enough, yeah. In probability theory, strictly positive density just means that no state in your system is absolutely 100% impossible.

07:08.920 --> 07:15.800
Everything has some non-zero probability of occurring, even if it's, like, infinitesimally small.

07:16.220 --> 07:18.660
Okay. So, no 0% chances.

07:18.900 --> 07:28.820
Right. And if your system has this property, the math will point to one, and exactly one, minimal set of variables that perfectly screens the inside from the outside.

07:29.040 --> 07:31.840
The boundary is mathematically undeniable and unique.

07:31.840 --> 07:37.960
But the paper explicitly states that this uniqueness breaks down if you lack strict positivity, right?

07:38.100 --> 07:41.400
And this is the third quirk, which is a massive landmine.

07:42.100 --> 07:47.580
If you have a situation where variables are deterministically linked, the boundary is no longer unique.

07:47.900 --> 07:50.540
By deterministic, you mean, like, locked together.

07:50.780 --> 07:51.160
Exactly.

07:51.320 --> 07:51.480
Right.

07:51.480 --> 07:55.520
It means if variable A happens, variable B happens, with 100% certainty.

07:55.920 --> 07:57.880
The probability is exactly 1.

07:58.400 --> 08:03.900
If A and B are perfectly equal all the time, and the third variable, C, depends on them,

08:04.420 --> 08:08.280
then you could say A is the blanket for C, or, you know, you could say B is the blanket for C.

08:08.440 --> 08:12.260
Because they carry the exact same information. They're functionally identical to the math.

08:12.480 --> 08:12.860
Exactly.

08:13.320 --> 08:17.080
The mathematics of the probability distribution just cannot select between them.

08:17.420 --> 08:20.200
There is no mathematical fact that privileges A over B.

08:20.200 --> 08:27.620
Hmm. So if I'm understanding this, um, if the math can't uniquely identify the boundary in a deterministic system,

08:27.620 --> 08:30.100
then the person doing the math has to make a choice.

08:30.840 --> 08:32.920
You're hitting on the core vulnerability right there.

08:33.620 --> 08:38.060
The mathematics is indifferent, which means the observer has to intervene and choose.

08:38.580 --> 08:41.560
But before we explore the consequences of the observer's choice,

08:41.880 --> 08:46.880
we really need to understand how we got from Judea Pearl's weather station statistics to biology.

08:46.880 --> 08:52.300
Yeah, how did a dry tool for updating beliefs become the theoretical skin of a living organism?

08:52.740 --> 08:56.320
Because if you look at the literature from the last 10 to 15 years,

08:56.420 --> 09:02.100
you have cognitive scientists and neuroscientists talking about Markov blankets as if they are tangible,

09:02.560 --> 09:05.660
like a cellular membrane or the skull protecting a brain.

09:05.660 --> 09:10.800
To understand the psychology and, honestly, the sociology of this leap,

09:11.140 --> 09:13.800
we have to look at the free energy principle literature.

09:14.420 --> 09:19.580
This is a massive body of work, heavily associated with the neuroscientist Karl Friston.

09:20.060 --> 09:20.280
Right.

09:20.960 --> 09:24.400
Biologists were grappling with a profound philosophical problem.

09:25.120 --> 09:30.320
How does a biological system maintain its integrity in a chaotic, entropic universe?

09:30.320 --> 09:35.280
Like, how does a cell not just dissolve into the puddle of water it's floating in?

09:35.640 --> 09:38.080
They needed a physical mechanism to explain separation.

09:38.380 --> 09:38.640
Yes.

09:39.180 --> 09:42.640
And they found Judea Pearl's Markov blanket and thought,

09:42.820 --> 09:43.640
this is it.

09:43.860 --> 09:46.420
This is the mathematical proof of separation.

09:47.280 --> 09:48.900
But to apply it to a living cell,

09:49.080 --> 09:54.240
they had to take Pearl's static, stationary graphical model and staple it onto dynamical systems.

09:54.820 --> 09:56.860
Systems that change and evolve over time,

09:57.040 --> 09:59.020
moving from a snapshot to a movie.

09:59.300 --> 09:59.760
Exactly.

10:00.460 --> 10:04.340
So, they started modeling organisms using stochastic differential equations.

10:05.060 --> 10:08.560
And they proposed a very specific four-part partition of the state space

10:08.560 --> 10:10.380
to represent a living thing.

10:10.580 --> 10:12.700
The famous four-part partition.

10:12.960 --> 10:14.520
Let's map this out for you, the listener,

10:14.660 --> 10:17.340
so you can visualize the biological model they built.

10:17.940 --> 10:20.440
We have four distinct classes of states.

10:20.880 --> 10:24.360
First, we have external states, denoted by the Greek letter eta.

10:24.960 --> 10:27.120
Then we have sensory states, which is S.

10:27.600 --> 10:29.500
We have active states, A.

10:29.760 --> 10:32.400
And finally, internal states, denoted by mu.

10:32.800 --> 10:34.400
So, mapping that to reality.

10:35.120 --> 10:37.600
The external states, eta, that's the environment.

10:38.180 --> 10:39.860
The puddle the cell is floating in.

10:40.540 --> 10:44.000
The internal states, mu, are the inner workings of the cell.

10:44.300 --> 10:45.800
It's metabolism, it's genetics.

10:46.000 --> 10:46.160
Okay.

10:46.160 --> 10:53.380
And the blanket itself, denoted as B, is defined as the combination of the sensory states and the active states.

10:53.380 --> 10:58.420
So, your senses and your actions form the wall between your inner mind and the outer world.

10:58.420 --> 10:59.260
That's the idea.

10:59.260 --> 11:05.940
And the defining requirement for this whole thing to be considered a distinct living entity, according to Friston and others,

11:05.940 --> 11:09.580
is the exact same conditional independence we talked about earlier.

11:09.580 --> 11:15.940
The external states are conditionally independent of the internal states, given the sensory and active states.

11:15.940 --> 11:17.780
And this raises an important question.

11:17.780 --> 11:22.120
Because here is where the massive philosophical leap happens.

11:22.120 --> 11:32.520
The core claim of the free energy principle literature is that because the internal states are conditionally independent of the external states, given the blanket,

11:33.160 --> 11:37.320
the interior has absolutely no direct access to the exterior.

11:37.320 --> 11:38.740
It's blind to it.

11:39.300 --> 11:39.980
Completely blind.

11:40.560 --> 11:48.140
Therefore, they argue, the only way the system can survive is if the interior maintains a cognitive model of the outside world,

11:48.720 --> 11:53.080
constantly updating that model based solely on the fluctuations it feels on the blanket.

11:53.460 --> 11:56.820
It's the ultimate brain in a vat scenario, right?

11:56.900 --> 11:58.320
But supposedly proven by math.

11:58.760 --> 12:02.940
The brain only knows the electrical signals coming through the wires, which is the blanket.

12:02.940 --> 12:10.780
But why did Friston and all these brilliant theoretical biologists assume this statistical condition was just naturally occurring in living things?

12:11.360 --> 12:15.520
Did it just intuitively feel right because of how physical objects work?

12:16.080 --> 12:18.220
It is entirely based on physical intuition, yeah.

12:19.480 --> 12:22.080
Specifically, a concept called sparse coupling.

12:23.300 --> 12:31.100
So, in a differential equation, coupling describes how one variable pushes or pulls on another as time moves forward.

12:31.100 --> 12:35.620
Sparse coupling means there are missing physical links.

12:36.420 --> 12:37.140
So, they don't touch.

12:37.440 --> 12:37.620
Right.

12:38.240 --> 12:42.120
The external states do not directly, physically, drive the internal states.

12:42.760 --> 12:46.260
The puddle of water doesn't directly mutate the cell's DNA.

12:46.760 --> 12:51.420
The outside only pushes on the sensors, and the inside only pushes on the actuators.

12:51.560 --> 12:53.840
They never physically touch each other directly.

12:54.220 --> 12:54.700
Precisely.

12:54.700 --> 13:03.980
And the literature looked at this missing physical link, this sparse coupling, and assumed, well, if they don't touch physically, they must be conditionally independent statistically.

13:04.560 --> 13:10.260
They conflated the physical wiring diagram of the system with the statistical probability distribution of the system.

13:10.260 --> 13:18.720
They assume that if the physical bridge is broken, the statistical correlation must also be zero, which intuitively sounds bulletproof.

13:18.720 --> 13:28.420
Like, if I am in a sealed concrete bunker, and I only have a radio to listen to and a microphone to speak into, I am physically sparsely coupled from the outside world.

13:28.900 --> 13:35.440
It feels entirely obvious that my internal thoughts are statistically independent of the outside world, given the state of the radio.

13:35.440 --> 13:41.600
It feels obvious, but the math says that intuition is profoundly, fundamentally flawed.

13:41.960 --> 13:46.240
And this brings us to the absolute core mathematical crux of Flyxion's paper.

13:46.740 --> 13:50.220
This is where the biological claims collide with rigorous calculus.

13:50.400 --> 13:53.120
We are going to dive deep into theorem one.

13:53.520 --> 13:56.960
Okay, if you're listening to this and you aren't a mathematician, do not panic.

13:57.520 --> 14:03.580
We are going to take this slow, and we are going to translate the matrix math into something you can actually visualize.

14:03.580 --> 14:09.060
Because theorem one is the reality check that tears the biological assumption to the ground.

14:09.640 --> 14:14.360
The paper examines a system evolving according to a linear stationary diffusion process.

14:14.780 --> 14:17.480
Right. Let's lay out the components of this mathematical engine.

14:18.020 --> 14:20.700
There are four critical objects we need to understand.

14:21.420 --> 14:24.080
First is the drift matrix, B.

14:24.840 --> 14:28.940
Think of the drift as the deterministic rules of the physical system.

14:28.940 --> 14:34.060
If you're a particle floating in a river, the drift is the physical current pulling you downstream.

14:34.520 --> 14:37.960
It's the direct physical pushing and pulling between variables.

14:38.740 --> 14:40.340
Okay, drift is the physical current?

14:40.740 --> 14:41.480
The physical coupling.

14:41.820 --> 14:42.200
Got it.

14:42.640 --> 14:44.680
Second is the diffusion matrix, D.

14:45.360 --> 14:48.160
This is the stochastic part, the random noise.

14:48.680 --> 14:50.760
If you know anything about Brownian motion,

14:51.420 --> 14:57.360
this is the unpredictable, erratic jostling of the water molecules hitting our particle from all sides.

14:57.360 --> 15:02.040
So drift is the steady current, and diffusion is the random jostling.

15:02.160 --> 15:02.300
Okay.

15:02.940 --> 15:06.600
Third is the stationary precision matrix, denoted by pi.

15:07.120 --> 15:09.560
This relates to the probability distribution.

15:10.080 --> 15:12.480
When you've let this system run for a very long time,

15:12.820 --> 15:17.120
it eventually settles into a stable overall shape, a stationary law.

15:17.760 --> 15:22.260
The precision matrix tells you how tightly clustered and correlated those probabilities are.

15:22.600 --> 15:24.640
And this is where we look for the blanket, right?

15:24.640 --> 15:30.240
Yes. If we are searching for our statistical Markov blanket, this is where we look.

15:30.900 --> 15:37.300
We want to see zeros in the specific blocks of this matrix that connect the inside to the outside.

15:37.940 --> 15:41.540
If the entry is zero, conditional independence is proven.

15:42.100 --> 15:45.400
So the precision matrix, pi, is the ultimate judge.

15:46.080 --> 15:47.440
Zeros mean the blanket is real.

15:48.020 --> 15:49.180
What is the fourth object?

15:49.180 --> 15:51.840
The fourth object is the wild card.

15:52.520 --> 15:54.760
It is the key to Friston's entire argument.

15:55.380 --> 15:59.060
It is the anti-symmetric circulation operator, Q.

15:59.480 --> 16:00.740
The circulation operator.

16:01.000 --> 16:02.800
What exactly is circulating?

16:03.220 --> 16:03.640
Energy.

16:04.300 --> 16:05.500
Probability current.

16:06.240 --> 16:10.820
In a system that is at total thermal equilibrium, a dead system like a rock,

16:11.240 --> 16:12.500
there is no net flow.

16:12.500 --> 16:17.540
But every single living organism is, by definition, out of equilibrium.

16:18.180 --> 16:21.360
Energy is constantly flowing in and out to sustain life.

16:21.720 --> 16:21.900
Right.

16:22.160 --> 16:22.800
Metabolism.

16:23.240 --> 16:23.600
Exactly.

16:24.160 --> 16:27.780
Even when the system's overall probability distribution looks stable,

16:28.240 --> 16:32.400
there is a constant swirling flow of probability current beneath the surface.

16:33.200 --> 16:37.800
Q represents the rotational circulating part of that out-of-equilibrium flow.

16:37.800 --> 16:38.620
OK.

16:38.980 --> 16:44.700
Now, theorem 1 in the paper connects these four objects together in one devastatingly simple formula.

16:45.280 --> 16:48.620
It's B equals D plus Q times pi.

16:49.020 --> 16:54.920
The drift equals the diffusion plus the circulation, all multiplied by the precision matrix.

16:55.900 --> 17:01.620
This equation is a revelation because it shows exactly where the biologists made their mistake.

17:02.340 --> 17:04.220
Let's break down the mistake.

17:04.220 --> 17:10.240
What happens if we apply this formula to a dead system, a system at equilibrium?

17:10.820 --> 17:13.600
In physics, equilibrium is called detailed balance.

17:14.080 --> 17:15.980
In detailed balance, there is no circulation.

17:16.740 --> 17:18.840
So Q is strictly zero.

17:19.400 --> 17:19.760
Oh, wow.

17:20.500 --> 17:23.720
So if Q is zero, the formula simplifies massively.

17:24.120 --> 17:30.800
The physical drift, B, is purely a function of the random diffusion, D, and the statistical precision, pi.

17:31.560 --> 17:32.000
Exactly.

17:32.000 --> 17:38.420
And in that specific dead detail balance scenario, the biological intuition is actually correct.

17:39.240 --> 17:43.940
Under detailed balance, sparse physical coupling, having zeros in your drift matrix,

17:44.600 --> 17:49.260
mathematically guarantees a statistical Markov blanket, zeros in your precision matrix.

17:49.760 --> 17:53.040
If they don't touch physically, they are statistically independent.

17:53.600 --> 17:56.620
But living systems are not dead.

17:57.220 --> 17:58.520
A living cell is an engine.

17:58.820 --> 18:01.080
A brain is a whirlwind of electrical activity.

18:01.080 --> 18:03.360
They are radically out of equilibrium.

18:04.020 --> 18:07.080
So for living things, Q is absolutely never zero.

18:07.480 --> 18:07.780
Precisely.

18:08.400 --> 18:16.100
And the instant Q is not zero, the equivalence between physical sparse coupling and statistical independence shatters completely.

18:17.040 --> 18:19.740
The circulation operator mixes everything up.

18:20.440 --> 18:24.900
Flyxion provides two incredibly detailed mathematical examples to prove exactly how this fails.

18:25.160 --> 18:26.180
In both directions.

18:26.180 --> 18:28.600
Here's where it gets really interesting.

18:29.360 --> 18:30.860
Let's walk through these examples.

18:31.220 --> 18:32.600
Let's look at example one first.

18:32.860 --> 18:34.400
I call this the false positive.

18:34.940 --> 18:38.060
I want to know exactly how the math betrays the physical intuition.

18:38.440 --> 18:40.300
Walk us through Flyxion's setup here.

18:40.300 --> 18:44.100
Okay, so Flyxion constructs a simple three-block linear system.

18:44.560 --> 18:49.900
We have our exterior environment, eta, our blanket, B, and our interior, mu.

18:50.320 --> 18:55.040
He sets the random diffusion, D, to be a basic uniform identity matrix.

18:55.700 --> 19:01.680
Then he specifically engineers the physical drift matrix, B, to perfectly mimic the biological ideal.

19:02.080 --> 19:03.100
He builds the bunker.

19:03.100 --> 19:04.140
He builds the bunker.

19:04.820 --> 19:09.900
He ensures there is absolutely no direct physical coupling between the exterior and the interior.

19:10.480 --> 19:14.620
The entries in the drift matrix connecting eta and mu are strictly zero.

19:15.160 --> 19:18.140
The inside and the outside never physically interact.

19:18.840 --> 19:23.480
So a biologist looking at this physical wiring diagram would immediately declare victory.

19:23.720 --> 19:25.500
They'd say, look, no physical connection.

19:25.780 --> 19:27.140
The cell is sparsely coupled.

19:27.560 --> 19:29.040
We have a Markov blanket.

19:29.040 --> 19:32.800
But then you have to calculate the statistical reality.

19:33.200 --> 19:35.000
You have to find the precision matrix pi.

19:35.420 --> 19:38.740
And the paper says you find this by solving the Lyapunov equation.

19:38.880 --> 19:40.900
Wait, let's not lose anyone in the weeds here.

19:41.040 --> 19:44.660
What is the Lyapunov equation actually doing in this context?

19:44.980 --> 19:47.980
It's a fundamental equation in control theory and dynamical systems.

19:48.520 --> 19:50.700
Without getting into the heavy algebra,

19:51.340 --> 19:54.320
the Lyapunov equation is basically a mathematical machine

19:54.320 --> 19:57.100
that lets you plug in the physical rules of the system.

19:57.100 --> 19:59.320
The drift and the randomness, the diffusion.

19:59.740 --> 20:02.760
And it spits out the final stable probability distribution,

20:03.160 --> 20:04.480
which is the precision matrix.

20:04.800 --> 20:07.120
It tells you where the system will eventually settle

20:07.120 --> 20:09.440
without you having to simulate it to infinity.

20:10.340 --> 20:14.380
Okay, so Flyxion runs this perfectly sparsely coupled system

20:14.380 --> 20:18.120
through the Lyapunov equation to find the statistical truth.

20:18.380 --> 20:19.460
What is the result?

20:19.620 --> 20:20.480
Does the blanket hold?

20:20.820 --> 20:24.000
The result is that because the system is out of equilibrium,

20:24.000 --> 20:26.920
it possesses a valid circulation operator.

20:27.100 --> 20:29.940
And because Q is mixing the currents,

20:30.380 --> 20:32.140
the resulting precision matrix, pi,

20:32.680 --> 20:35.940
does not have zeros between the inside and the outside.

20:36.620 --> 20:38.520
The math in the paper is explicit.

20:38.740 --> 20:40.960
The entry in the precision matrix,

20:41.680 --> 20:43.460
pi sub eta mu,

20:43.580 --> 20:47.180
is exactly 74 divided by 1273,

20:47.680 --> 20:49.960
which is roughly 0.058.

20:50.000 --> 20:51.220
It is not zero.

20:51.220 --> 20:53.120
Which means that statistically,

20:53.740 --> 20:56.640
the internal and external coordinates are conditionally dependent,

20:57.240 --> 20:59.220
even though neither physical state drives the other.

20:59.980 --> 21:02.080
The sparse physical coupling completely failed

21:02.080 --> 21:03.860
to create a statistical Markov blanket.

21:04.240 --> 21:07.800
If you're listening and struggling to map the matrices to reality,

21:08.220 --> 21:09.460
let me try out an analogy.

21:10.060 --> 21:14.140
Let's ground B, D, Q, and pi in a physical scenario.

21:14.700 --> 21:17.600
Think of a massive multi-lane traffic roundabout.

21:17.600 --> 21:18.980
Oh, I like where this is going.

21:19.160 --> 21:21.260
You have cars entering the roundabout from the north.

21:21.540 --> 21:25.040
Let's call the north the exterior environment, eta.

21:25.440 --> 21:27.360
And you have cars entering from the south,

21:27.680 --> 21:29.180
that's the interior, mu.

21:29.800 --> 21:33.540
The circular road of the roundabout itself is the blanket, B.

21:34.080 --> 21:35.620
Okay, the physical structure is set.

21:36.120 --> 21:38.660
The physical asphalt lanes that guide the cars,

21:38.940 --> 21:40.640
that's our drift matrix, B.

21:41.180 --> 21:43.900
Notice that the north entry lane and the south entry lane

21:43.900 --> 21:45.760
never physically touch each other.

21:45.760 --> 21:47.400
They are sparsely coupled.

21:47.980 --> 21:49.760
A car entering from the north is not directly,

21:50.720 --> 21:52.740
physically pushing a car entering from the south.

21:53.140 --> 21:53.200
Right.

21:53.680 --> 21:55.980
And the drivers swerving randomly in their lanes,

21:56.320 --> 21:57.640
checking their phones, adjusting the radio,

21:57.800 --> 21:59.540
that's the random diffusion, D?

22:00.040 --> 22:00.520
Exactly.

22:01.200 --> 22:03.060
Now, if this were just a parking lot,

22:03.220 --> 22:06.000
a system at equilibrium, detailed balance,

22:06.260 --> 22:08.680
the positions of the north cars and south cars

22:08.680 --> 22:10.260
would be statistically independent.

22:10.720 --> 22:14.000
But a roundabout is an out-of-equilibrium system.

22:14.000 --> 22:17.040
It has a continuous swirling flow of traffic.

22:17.880 --> 22:22.280
That constant circular momentum is our circulation operator, Q.

22:22.920 --> 22:24.720
So what happens to the statistics?

22:25.580 --> 22:26.960
What does the pie matrix look like?

22:27.180 --> 22:29.660
The statistics are the precision matrix, Pi.

22:30.180 --> 22:33.940
Imagine taking a time-lapse aerial photograph of the roundabout

22:33.940 --> 22:36.740
to see where cars most likely end up.

22:36.740 --> 22:40.020
Because of that continuous circulation, Q,

22:40.300 --> 22:42.660
a massive traffic jam entering from the north

22:42.660 --> 22:44.520
is going to bleed into the roundabout

22:44.520 --> 22:46.660
and eventually disrupt the flow of cars

22:46.660 --> 22:48.000
trying to enter from the south.

22:48.380 --> 22:52.600
The continuous circular flow creates a statistical correlation,

22:52.920 --> 22:55.600
a dependency between the north and south,

22:56.020 --> 22:58.820
completely bypassing the fact that they never physically touched.

22:58.820 --> 23:03.140
The circulation, Q, creates a statistical dependency, Pi,

23:03.700 --> 23:07.100
that the physical wiring diagram, B, completely conceals.

23:07.220 --> 23:07.740
Exactly.

23:08.260 --> 23:10.460
That is a phenomenal way to visualize it.

23:10.980 --> 23:13.380
You cannot look at the physical connections, the drift,

23:13.800 --> 23:16.500
to determine the statistical reality, the precision,

23:17.000 --> 23:19.420
when a system is swirling out of equilibrium.

23:20.060 --> 23:23.960
The out-of-equilibrium flow acts as a hidden bridge for information.

23:24.640 --> 23:27.280
That's example one, the false positive.

23:27.840 --> 23:29.920
Now let's blow our minds with example two,

23:30.460 --> 23:32.980
the false negative, because this one goes the other way.

23:33.600 --> 23:36.080
In example two, Flyxion reverses the engineering.

23:36.680 --> 23:38.660
He starts by forcing the system to have

23:38.660 --> 23:41.400
a mathematically perfect statistical Markov blanket.

23:41.980 --> 23:44.360
He manually designs the precision matrix Pi

23:44.360 --> 23:48.400
so that the entry connecting the inside and outside is exactly zero,

23:49.060 --> 23:50.600
Pi sub eta mu equals zero.

23:50.600 --> 23:55.940
And he also designs a valid, out-of-equilibrium circulation matrix, Q.

23:56.520 --> 23:58.820
So statistically, we have the holy grail.

23:59.160 --> 24:02.280
The interior is flawlessly screened from the exterior.

24:02.980 --> 24:05.660
Yes, but then, using our master formula,

24:05.840 --> 24:07.940
B equals D plus Q times Pi,

24:08.360 --> 24:12.140
he works backward to calculate what the physical drift matrix, B,

24:12.780 --> 24:15.860
must look like to support this perfect statistical blanket.

24:15.860 --> 24:19.220
The result is completely counterintuitive.

24:20.560 --> 24:24.440
The drift entries connecting the exterior and the interior are not zero.

24:25.320 --> 24:27.680
The paper notes they are two and negative two.

24:28.360 --> 24:32.220
Meaning the outside is directly, physically pushing on the inside,

24:32.360 --> 24:34.460
and the inside is directly pulling on the outside.

24:34.840 --> 24:37.100
They are physically manhandling each other.

24:37.420 --> 24:39.560
They are intimately, physically coupled.

24:39.560 --> 24:43.260
And yet, despite this direct physical interaction,

24:43.880 --> 24:47.760
the precise interplay between the random diffusion and the swirling circulation

24:47.760 --> 24:50.520
perfectly cancels out the statistical correlation.

24:51.120 --> 24:55.740
They maintain a perfect statistical Markov blanket while physically interacting.

24:56.260 --> 24:59.420
This completely upends the biological paradigm.

24:59.820 --> 25:02.120
To confirm this clearly for the listener,

25:02.120 --> 25:05.820
The sparse coupling that Friston and theoretical biologists

25:05.820 --> 25:09.220
constantly use to justify the physical existence of a boundary

25:09.220 --> 25:11.960
is neither necessary nor sufficient

25:11.960 --> 25:16.180
for a statistical Markov blanket to actually exist in a living system.

25:16.400 --> 25:19.840
That is the inescapable conclusion of theorem one.

25:20.560 --> 25:23.600
It is a devastating blow to the casual use of this mathematics.

25:24.340 --> 25:27.740
You cannot look at a sparsely coupled physical cell and declare,

25:28.160 --> 25:30.140
therefore it has a statistical blanket.

25:30.140 --> 25:33.480
And you cannot look at a statistical blanket and declare,

25:33.820 --> 25:35.760
therefore the system is physically isolated.

25:36.020 --> 25:36.860
It's just not true.

25:37.100 --> 25:40.320
The mathematical reality is that the blanket condition only holds

25:40.320 --> 25:43.220
when the physical drift, the random diffusion,

25:43.820 --> 25:45.540
the out-of-equilibrium circulation,

25:45.940 --> 25:50.460
and the statistical precision are all jointly, exquisitely synchronized.

25:51.100 --> 25:55.000
It is an assumption, but a highly specific harmony in the dynamics.

25:55.240 --> 25:58.560
It is not an automatic consequence of things not touching.

25:58.560 --> 26:02.040
Okay, so if the math is completely agnostic about physical space,

26:02.540 --> 26:04.760
if sparse coupling doesn't guarantee a boundary,

26:05.340 --> 26:07.800
what exactly is the blanket bounding?

26:08.020 --> 26:11.220
I mean, if it's not a natural, objective, physical wall, what is it?

26:11.700 --> 26:15.340
This is where the paper shifts from physics into epistemology.

26:15.860 --> 26:19.400
It turns out the existence of the boundary depends almost entirely on

26:19.400 --> 26:21.840
who is holding the pen and drawing the graph.

26:21.840 --> 26:26.300
Wow. The paper introduces a mathematical proof called Proposition 1.

26:26.840 --> 26:29.600
It states that conditional independence survives, quote,

26:29.840 --> 26:34.180
block-wise bijections, but fails completely if you mix blocks.

26:34.660 --> 26:37.580
We need to explain this because the implications are wild.

26:37.580 --> 26:39.580
Let's translate the math.

26:39.780 --> 26:43.720
A bijection is just a formal term for a mathematical mapping

26:43.720 --> 26:48.060
that relabels or transforms variables without losing any underlying information.

26:48.220 --> 26:49.520
It's a perfect translation.

26:50.540 --> 26:54.200
Proposition 1 says that if you have a perfect Markov blanket

26:54.200 --> 26:58.640
and you apply a mathematical transformation only to the internal variables

26:58.640 --> 27:02.760
or only to the external variables, the blanket survives.

27:03.080 --> 27:05.180
You haven't broken the conditional independence.

27:05.180 --> 27:09.100
So if I decide to measure the internal temperature of the cell in Celsius

27:09.100 --> 27:11.780
instead of Fahrenheit, the blanket still exists.

27:12.180 --> 27:12.620
Exactly.

27:13.420 --> 27:16.460
Block-wise relabeling preserves the statistical screening.

27:17.220 --> 27:19.860
But the moment you apply a mathematical transformation

27:19.860 --> 27:23.620
that mixes variables from the inside with variables from the outside,

27:24.200 --> 27:26.720
the conditional independence is completely annihilated.

27:27.040 --> 27:30.740
Phlygesen gives a geometric example of this in the paper that is just beautiful.

27:31.140 --> 27:34.180
If you're listening, imagine a standard piece of graph paper.

27:34.180 --> 27:38.220
You have a simple zero-mean Gaussian probability law.

27:38.460 --> 27:41.140
Imagine a cloud of dots on the graph paper.

27:41.480 --> 27:44.740
You have an exterior variable on the horizontal x-axis,

27:45.220 --> 27:47.600
an interior variable on the vertical y-axis.

27:48.160 --> 27:50.620
The math shows that they are conditionally independent.

27:50.960 --> 27:52.400
A trivial blanket exists.

27:52.780 --> 27:55.960
What's fascinating here is what Flyxion asks next.

27:56.220 --> 27:59.220
What happens if you simply rotate the coordinate plane?

27:59.220 --> 28:02.720
If you physically rotate the graph paper by an angle, theta,

28:03.000 --> 28:05.000
you are essentially creating new axes.

28:05.560 --> 28:12.080
These new x- and y-axis are now a mathematical mix of the old inside and the old outside.

28:12.240 --> 28:13.940
Because they're slanted across both.

28:14.080 --> 28:14.560
Exactly.

28:15.380 --> 28:16.960
And the moment you do that rotation,

28:17.420 --> 28:18.860
for almost any generic angle,

28:19.380 --> 28:21.320
the conditional independence vanishes.

28:21.960 --> 28:24.840
The math suddenly shows that the variables are highly dependent.

28:24.840 --> 28:29.140
Just by looking at the exact same cloud of dots from a tilted angle.

28:29.700 --> 28:32.200
Literally just by rotating the lens of observation.

28:33.060 --> 28:34.360
The blanket vanishes.

28:35.280 --> 28:38.320
This is incontrovertible mathematical proof

28:38.320 --> 28:42.300
that the Markov blanket is not a property of the physical system taken alone.

28:42.560 --> 28:46.800
It is a property of a description alongside a probability law.

28:47.040 --> 28:49.820
That is a massive paradigm shift.

28:49.820 --> 28:53.820
The boundary isn't an objective physical wall in the universe.

28:54.000 --> 28:57.980
It's a feature of how you, the scientist, choose to measure the system.

28:58.800 --> 29:01.040
The paper also brings up coarse graining,

29:01.340 --> 29:03.440
which takes this subjectivity even further.

29:03.800 --> 29:05.680
Coarse graining is the act of zooming out.

29:06.380 --> 29:10.760
It is deliberately merging variables together to simplify a complex model.

29:10.760 --> 29:14.220
If you have a highly detailed, fine-grained system

29:14.220 --> 29:16.900
where absolutely no Markov blanket exists,

29:17.460 --> 29:20.120
everything is statistically tangled with everything else.

29:20.660 --> 29:24.880
The paper points out that if you selectively merge certain variables together,

29:25.500 --> 29:27.420
if you deliberately throw away some information,

29:27.780 --> 29:31.220
you can magically create a statistical Markov blanket

29:31.220 --> 29:33.300
where none existed a moment ago.

29:33.800 --> 29:36.780
You can literally invent a mathematical boundary just by squinting.

29:36.960 --> 29:37.160
Yes.

29:37.160 --> 29:41.560
The act of merging variables can manufacture the conditional independence.

29:42.540 --> 29:46.640
Therefore, the statement that a system has a Markov blanket

29:46.640 --> 29:49.540
has absolutely zero determinate truth value

29:49.540 --> 29:53.660
unless you explicitly specify exactly which variables you are measuring

29:53.660 --> 29:57.400
and at what scale or grain of observation.

29:57.880 --> 29:59.160
If you are listening to this right now,

29:59.220 --> 30:02.400
I want you to realize how disruptive this is to modern science news.

30:02.860 --> 30:05.420
Right now, there are countless pop science articles

30:05.420 --> 30:09.280
and academic papers claiming that the human brain has a Markov blanket

30:09.280 --> 30:12.160
or a single neuron has a Markov blanket.

30:12.300 --> 30:16.580
And therefore, it is a distinct, conscious entity that models the world.

30:16.960 --> 30:19.800
But, based on Proposition 1 and coarse graining,

30:20.340 --> 30:22.420
you have to immediately ask those scientists,

30:22.960 --> 30:23.740
at what scale?

30:24.540 --> 30:28.060
Are we drawing the boundary at the level of neurotransmitter molecules?

30:28.700 --> 30:29.480
Single neurons?

30:29.900 --> 30:30.680
Cortical columns?

30:31.140 --> 30:32.420
The entire frontal lobe?

30:32.420 --> 30:35.960
Because, depending on how the scientist chooses to group the variables,

30:36.200 --> 30:37.980
the math changes entirely.

30:38.300 --> 30:41.840
The universe doesn't select the physically relevant boundary.

30:42.100 --> 30:42.880
The scientist does.

30:43.580 --> 30:44.340
The math is neutral.

30:44.600 --> 30:45.700
It's just a lens.

30:46.460 --> 30:47.440
As Flyxion writes,

30:47.760 --> 30:49.360
the blanket attaches to a description,

30:49.760 --> 30:50.760
not a physical object.

30:51.420 --> 30:53.400
If you claim a physical boundary exists,

30:53.480 --> 30:55.080
you cannot just point to the math and say,

30:55.240 --> 30:56.460
the equation proved it.

30:56.460 --> 30:59.360
You have to provide an outside, physical argument

30:59.360 --> 31:01.840
for why your specific chosen description

31:01.840 --> 31:05.540
is physically privileged over all the other possible descriptions.

31:05.860 --> 31:09.020
Which naturally leads us to a massive biological hurdle.

31:09.400 --> 31:12.600
If a blanket is just a matter of subjective description,

31:12.860 --> 31:15.440
if it depends entirely on who drew the graph

31:15.440 --> 31:16.860
and how far they zoomed in,

31:17.240 --> 31:19.360
how in the world does a biologist define

31:19.360 --> 31:21.960
an actual living, breathing individual?

31:21.960 --> 31:24.300
Because, clearly, I am physically separate

31:24.300 --> 31:26.060
from the microphone I am speaking into.

31:27.320 --> 31:29.280
This is where Flyxion addresses a very public,

31:29.520 --> 31:30.220
ongoing debate

31:30.220 --> 31:32.500
that was recently highlighted by researchers

31:32.500 --> 31:34.780
like Mark Solms and Kurt Giamengal.

31:35.820 --> 31:38.360
They recognize this exact problem of scale

31:38.360 --> 31:39.460
and arbitrary boundaries.

31:40.080 --> 31:42.600
To defend the biological use of Markov blankets,

31:42.860 --> 31:45.480
they rely on the concept of nested blankets.

31:45.740 --> 31:45.980
Right.

31:46.200 --> 31:48.220
They argue that nature itself is organized

31:48.220 --> 31:49.560
in a nested hierarchy.

31:49.560 --> 31:51.900
You have macromolecules that possess

31:51.900 --> 31:53.300
their own Markov blankets.

31:53.720 --> 31:55.960
Those molecules make up organelles,

31:56.340 --> 31:57.060
which have blankets,

31:57.620 --> 31:59.380
which make up cells with blankets,

31:59.920 --> 32:00.980
organs with blankets,

32:01.100 --> 32:02.880
all the way up to entire organisms.

32:03.380 --> 32:06.220
It's Russian nesting dolls of statistical boundaries.

32:06.760 --> 32:07.820
And their core argument is that

32:07.820 --> 32:10.480
to find the true boundary of an individual subject,

32:10.880 --> 32:13.320
to find where the human being actually exists,

32:13.980 --> 32:15.880
you look for the level in that hierarchy

32:15.880 --> 32:17.740
where the survival of the parts

32:17.740 --> 32:20.680
is delegated to the functioning of the whole.

32:21.020 --> 32:23.180
They call this delegated viability.

32:23.700 --> 32:25.800
Let me make sure I grasp delegated viability.

32:26.280 --> 32:28.460
It's the idea that a single skin cell on my arm

32:28.460 --> 32:30.940
doesn't have true independent agency

32:30.940 --> 32:32.400
or viability in the wild.

32:33.020 --> 32:34.440
It has delegated its survival

32:34.440 --> 32:36.340
to the larger system of my body.

32:36.760 --> 32:38.180
My heart pumps the blood,

32:38.360 --> 32:39.600
my lungs get the oxygen,

32:39.860 --> 32:41.520
and my skin cell survives

32:41.520 --> 32:44.060
purely because the whole organism survives.

32:44.060 --> 32:46.360
If the organism dies, the cell dies.

32:46.940 --> 32:47.360
Exactly.

32:47.980 --> 32:51.120
And conversely, if a cell stops deferring to the whole,

32:51.420 --> 32:53.600
if it ignores the blanket of the organism

32:53.600 --> 32:55.220
and starts acting entirely

32:55.220 --> 32:58.040
for its own immediate, unchecked, local replication,

32:58.480 --> 33:00.040
we call that a malignancy,

33:00.320 --> 33:01.160
and we call it cancer.

33:01.840 --> 33:03.180
It endangers the whole system

33:03.180 --> 33:05.340
and ultimately destroys itself.

33:06.300 --> 33:08.060
So, Solmes and others argue

33:08.060 --> 33:10.220
that the true boundary of the self

33:10.220 --> 33:12.100
is the outermost blanket

33:12.100 --> 33:15.060
where this biological viability is delegated.

33:15.940 --> 33:17.340
It sounds incredibly profound.

33:17.960 --> 33:20.280
It intuitively makes perfect sense

33:20.280 --> 33:21.600
of how biology works,

33:21.720 --> 33:23.380
but what does Flycore say

33:23.380 --> 33:25.340
about how this relates to the statistics

33:25.340 --> 33:26.400
we've been talking about?

33:27.100 --> 33:28.220
Flycore's rigorous take

33:28.220 --> 33:29.740
is that delegated viability

33:29.740 --> 33:31.720
is a beautiful, deeply compelling

33:31.720 --> 33:33.060
biological hypothesis.

33:33.540 --> 33:35.920
But the statistical Markov blanket

33:35.920 --> 33:37.340
does absolutely nothing

33:37.340 --> 33:39.420
to supply or prove this condition.

33:39.420 --> 33:40.900
The math doesn't care.

33:41.180 --> 33:42.280
The math is blind to it.

33:42.820 --> 33:44.240
The stationary probability law,

33:44.340 --> 33:46.940
the precision matrix pi we spent so much time on,

33:47.280 --> 33:49.880
has zero concept of delegated viability.

33:50.540 --> 33:51.960
The math doesn't know what life is.

33:52.020 --> 33:53.060
It doesn't know what death is.

33:53.400 --> 33:56.100
It only sees conditional statistical independence.

33:56.720 --> 33:57.040
Right.

33:57.640 --> 33:59.740
If you have a nested family of partitions,

34:00.000 --> 34:01.540
all satisfying a blanket condition

34:01.540 --> 34:03.480
at their own specific zoomed in

34:03.480 --> 34:04.460
or zoomed out scale,

34:05.080 --> 34:06.720
the stationary law cannot tell you

34:06.720 --> 34:08.020
which level of that nest

34:08.020 --> 34:09.680
warrants the title of subject.

34:10.080 --> 34:11.540
It doesn't tell you if the single cell

34:11.540 --> 34:13.120
is the individual or the liver

34:13.120 --> 34:13.860
or the human

34:13.860 --> 34:16.480
or the entire ecological forest system.

34:16.660 --> 34:18.100
The paper points out something

34:18.100 --> 34:19.500
really fascinating here

34:19.500 --> 34:21.920
about the commensurability of needs

34:21.920 --> 34:23.200
when it comes to survival.

34:23.660 --> 34:25.180
This feels really important.

34:25.440 --> 34:26.700
This is a crucial flaw

34:26.700 --> 34:28.240
in how some models apply the math.

34:28.940 --> 34:30.780
When we talk about viability,

34:31.100 --> 34:32.340
we are talking about an organism

34:32.340 --> 34:34.960
fulfilling multiple distinct critical needs.

34:35.860 --> 34:37.460
An animal needs oxygen,

34:38.220 --> 34:38.460
water,

34:39.080 --> 34:39.380
food,

34:40.360 --> 34:42.020
and specific temperature regulation.

34:42.020 --> 34:42.420
Right.

34:42.580 --> 34:43.500
Lots of different inputs.

34:44.420 --> 34:46.400
But the mathematics of active inference

34:46.400 --> 34:47.840
often tries to boil

34:47.840 --> 34:49.200
all of this complex survival

34:49.200 --> 34:50.200
down to a single

34:50.200 --> 34:52.020
scalar objective,

34:52.480 --> 34:53.900
a single number to minimize,

34:54.100 --> 34:56.040
like free energy or surprise.

34:56.380 --> 34:57.520
It treats survival

34:57.520 --> 34:59.140
like a video game health bar,

34:59.300 --> 35:00.500
just one single number

35:00.500 --> 35:01.300
going up or down.

35:01.580 --> 35:01.920
Exactly.

35:03.000 --> 35:04.020
But Flyxion argues

35:04.020 --> 35:05.000
that the physical needs

35:05.000 --> 35:05.620
of an organism

35:05.620 --> 35:07.740
are not always commensurable.

35:08.440 --> 35:11.020
You cannot mathematically compensate

35:11.020 --> 35:12.980
across indispensable requirements.

35:13.880 --> 35:15.120
A single scalar objective

35:15.120 --> 35:16.460
can completely hide

35:16.460 --> 35:17.860
a fatal biological flaw.

35:18.340 --> 35:18.740
How so?

35:19.280 --> 35:21.020
Your overall survival score

35:21.020 --> 35:22.860
might look mathematically fantastic

35:22.860 --> 35:24.520
because you have a massive,

35:24.800 --> 35:26.200
overwhelming abundance of oxygen,

35:26.620 --> 35:28.300
which completely masks the fact

35:28.300 --> 35:29.540
that you are actively dying

35:29.540 --> 35:30.320
of dehydration.

35:31.200 --> 35:31.800
Equal deficits

35:31.800 --> 35:32.900
of two different needs

35:32.900 --> 35:35.140
do not mathematically sum

35:35.140 --> 35:35.800
to a quantity

35:35.800 --> 35:36.500
that can be fixed

35:36.500 --> 35:37.580
by over-satisfying

35:37.580 --> 35:38.220
just one of them.

35:38.920 --> 35:40.040
So if I'm wandering the desert,

35:40.460 --> 35:41.200
starving to death,

35:41.980 --> 35:43.180
breathing twice as deeply

35:43.180 --> 35:44.720
doesn't save my life.

35:44.960 --> 35:45.320
Exactly.

35:45.720 --> 35:47.320
And the statistical Markov blanket

35:47.320 --> 35:48.200
has no metric

35:48.200 --> 35:49.560
for combining or weighting

35:49.560 --> 35:50.580
these indispensable

35:50.580 --> 35:51.720
physical constraints.

35:52.240 --> 35:54.020
It provides absolutely no rules

35:54.020 --> 35:55.860
for how to balance thirst

35:55.860 --> 35:56.820
against oxygen.

35:56.820 --> 35:59.120
The blanket can certainly

35:59.120 --> 36:00.780
act as a statistical interface

36:00.780 --> 36:02.200
to monitor these variables,

36:02.400 --> 36:04.600
but the statistical screening alone

36:04.600 --> 36:05.580
doesn't establish

36:05.580 --> 36:06.640
the rules of survival.

36:06.640 --> 36:08.460
So to synthesize this,

36:08.900 --> 36:09.760
we are sneaking

36:09.760 --> 36:11.200
our biological intuition

36:11.200 --> 36:12.140
through the back door

36:12.140 --> 36:13.140
and pretending

36:13.140 --> 36:14.500
it is a mathematical proof.

36:15.300 --> 36:16.120
Delegated viability

36:16.120 --> 36:17.860
is a completely valid way

36:17.860 --> 36:18.920
to define an organism,

36:18.920 --> 36:20.440
but it is an addition

36:20.440 --> 36:21.640
to the mathematics.

36:21.640 --> 36:23.700
It is a biological constraint

36:23.700 --> 36:24.360
that the scientist

36:24.360 --> 36:26.340
is forcing onto the equations

36:26.340 --> 36:27.180
from the outside.

36:27.900 --> 36:28.840
You cannot derive

36:28.840 --> 36:30.240
the concept of an organism

36:30.240 --> 36:31.700
dying simply from the fact

36:31.700 --> 36:33.200
that a cross-block entry

36:33.200 --> 36:34.340
in a precision matrix

36:34.340 --> 36:35.280
happens to be zero.

36:35.620 --> 36:36.780
That is the precise

36:36.780 --> 36:37.960
philosophical trap

36:37.960 --> 36:39.340
Flyxion is exposing.

36:39.940 --> 36:41.640
The mathematical formalism

36:41.640 --> 36:42.620
of the Markov blanket

36:42.620 --> 36:44.460
does not deliver the concept

36:44.460 --> 36:45.940
of an individual subject.

36:46.220 --> 36:47.600
Okay, we have covered

36:47.600 --> 36:48.440
spatial boundaries,

36:49.080 --> 36:50.600
the illusion of physical coupling,

36:50.600 --> 36:52.100
how boundaries are

36:52.100 --> 36:53.100
entirely relative

36:53.100 --> 36:53.840
to the observer,

36:54.260 --> 36:55.660
and how survival metrics

36:55.660 --> 36:56.520
aren't inherent

36:56.520 --> 36:57.300
in the statistics.

36:57.560 --> 36:58.660
That is a lot

36:58.660 --> 36:59.920
of shattered assumptions.

37:00.380 --> 37:01.920
But now we have to look

37:01.920 --> 37:02.460
at the dimension

37:02.460 --> 37:03.820
that messes everything up

37:03.820 --> 37:04.380
even further,

37:04.680 --> 37:05.780
which is time.

37:06.180 --> 37:06.500
Time changes

37:06.500 --> 37:07.440
the entire equation.

37:07.700 --> 37:09.160
We have to look at asynchrony

37:09.160 --> 37:11.280
and the completion problem.

37:11.680 --> 37:12.460
The paper makes

37:12.460 --> 37:14.600
a massive disciplinary shift here.

37:14.720 --> 37:15.360
It moves away

37:15.360 --> 37:16.440
from the continuous

37:16.440 --> 37:17.880
biological diffusion

37:17.880 --> 37:18.760
we just talked about,

37:19.080 --> 37:20.160
the fluid dynamics

37:20.160 --> 37:21.560
of cells and whirlpools,

37:21.560 --> 37:22.540
and moves over

37:22.540 --> 37:23.820
into computer science.

37:24.500 --> 37:24.940
Specifically,

37:25.140 --> 37:26.080
the paper introduces

37:26.080 --> 37:27.080
Karl Fant's

37:27.080 --> 37:28.440
null convention logic

37:28.440 --> 37:30.060
and the invocation model

37:30.060 --> 37:30.640
of computing.

37:31.260 --> 37:32.060
If we connect this

37:32.060 --> 37:32.860
to the bigger picture,

37:33.280 --> 37:34.060
this section is about

37:34.060 --> 37:35.240
how complex systems

37:35.240 --> 37:36.860
actually process information

37:36.860 --> 37:38.620
in physical reality,

37:38.820 --> 37:39.640
as opposed to how

37:39.640 --> 37:40.320
they process it

37:40.320 --> 37:41.700
in a timeless,

37:41.980 --> 37:43.340
perfect mathematical equation.

37:43.920 --> 37:44.900
Most of the free energy

37:44.900 --> 37:45.720
principle literature

37:45.720 --> 37:46.780
assumes a continuous,

37:46.780 --> 37:49.240
perfectly smooth flow of time,

37:49.580 --> 37:51.320
or at least a perfectly

37:51.320 --> 37:52.560
synchronized metronome

37:52.560 --> 37:53.800
ticking in the background

37:53.800 --> 37:54.500
of the universe.

37:55.200 --> 37:57.060
But real biological systems

37:57.060 --> 37:58.300
and advanced logical

37:58.300 --> 37:59.100
computing systems

37:59.100 --> 37:59.760
like FANs

37:59.760 --> 38:00.960
are asynchronous.

38:00.960 --> 38:02.300
Let's make sure

38:02.300 --> 38:03.300
we clearly distinguish

38:03.300 --> 38:04.280
between synchronous

38:04.280 --> 38:06.080
and asynchronous systems.

38:06.780 --> 38:08.140
A traditional laptop computer

38:08.140 --> 38:09.120
has a global clock.

38:09.440 --> 38:10.660
Tick, tock, tick, tock,

38:10.740 --> 38:12.380
billions of times a second.

38:12.980 --> 38:13.500
Every single

38:13.500 --> 38:14.480
microchip component

38:14.480 --> 38:15.780
updates at the exact

38:15.780 --> 38:16.620
same moment

38:16.620 --> 38:17.260
on the tick.

38:17.420 --> 38:18.300
Right, that's synchronous.

38:19.000 --> 38:20.400
But an asynchronous system

38:20.400 --> 38:21.080
doesn't have

38:21.080 --> 38:21.900
a global conductor

38:21.900 --> 38:22.720
waving a baton.

38:22.980 --> 38:24.100
So how does it

38:24.100 --> 38:25.040
know when to act?

38:25.380 --> 38:26.580
It relies entirely

38:26.580 --> 38:27.880
on local completion.

38:28.440 --> 38:29.240
In FANs' model

38:29.240 --> 38:29.820
of computing,

38:30.460 --> 38:31.560
computation is organized

38:31.560 --> 38:32.420
by alternating

38:32.420 --> 38:33.700
data wavefronts

38:33.700 --> 38:35.020
and null wavefronts.

38:35.720 --> 38:36.860
A process element,

38:37.020 --> 38:37.540
whether that's

38:37.540 --> 38:39.080
a silicon logical gate

38:39.080 --> 38:40.760
or a biological neuron,

38:41.200 --> 38:42.140
only fires

38:42.140 --> 38:43.440
or updates its state

38:43.440 --> 38:44.380
when it receives

38:44.380 --> 38:45.460
a definitive signal

38:45.460 --> 38:46.260
that its inputs

38:46.260 --> 38:47.500
are physically complete

38:47.500 --> 38:48.080
and ready.

38:48.600 --> 38:49.920
It waits for the full

38:49.920 --> 38:51.840
data phase to arrive.

38:52.500 --> 38:52.900
And then what?

38:53.320 --> 38:54.080
Once it processes

38:54.080 --> 38:54.620
that data,

38:55.000 --> 38:55.800
it resets into

38:55.800 --> 38:56.560
a null state,

38:56.860 --> 38:57.460
which indicates

38:57.460 --> 38:58.660
the absence of a value

38:58.660 --> 38:59.620
and it simply

38:59.620 --> 39:00.200
waits again.

39:00.980 --> 39:01.300
Just a bunch

39:01.300 --> 39:02.200
of localized actors

39:02.200 --> 39:02.720
saying,

39:03.360 --> 39:04.180
okay, I have all

39:04.180 --> 39:04.700
my ingredients

39:04.700 --> 39:05.320
from my neighbors,

39:05.560 --> 39:06.080
I'm going to bake

39:06.080 --> 39:06.760
the cake now,

39:07.280 --> 39:07.740
done,

39:08.120 --> 39:08.740
now I'm waiting

39:08.740 --> 39:09.620
for more ingredients.

39:10.000 --> 39:10.420
Exactly.

39:10.800 --> 39:11.740
And this introduces

39:11.740 --> 39:13.440
a massive structural

39:13.440 --> 39:14.360
problem for the

39:14.360 --> 39:15.580
Markov blanket concept.

39:16.020 --> 39:17.200
Because when dealing

39:17.200 --> 39:18.500
with asynchronous time,

39:18.920 --> 39:19.840
we have to distinguish

39:19.840 --> 39:20.720
between two

39:20.720 --> 39:22.200
completely different concepts,

39:22.940 --> 39:23.400
screening

39:23.400 --> 39:24.900
and completion.

39:25.280 --> 39:26.080
Let's define them.

39:26.080 --> 39:27.920
Screening is what

39:27.920 --> 39:28.480
we've been talking

39:28.480 --> 39:29.320
about this whole time,

39:29.720 --> 39:31.120
the statistical condition

39:31.120 --> 39:32.460
on the stationary law.

39:32.920 --> 39:33.700
The fact that,

39:34.020 --> 39:34.620
on average,

39:34.820 --> 39:35.720
the blanket completely

39:35.720 --> 39:37.140
hides the outside world

39:37.140 --> 39:37.960
from the inside.

39:38.220 --> 39:38.520
Right.

39:38.960 --> 39:39.740
But completion

39:39.740 --> 39:41.100
is the physical

39:41.100 --> 39:42.680
chronological requirement

39:42.680 --> 39:44.140
that the internal system

39:44.140 --> 39:45.420
only updates and acts

39:45.420 --> 39:46.760
when every single

39:46.760 --> 39:48.040
component of its blanket

39:48.040 --> 39:49.580
has successfully reached

39:49.580 --> 39:50.740
the data phase.

39:51.460 --> 39:52.740
The state consumed

39:52.740 --> 39:53.720
by the interior

39:53.720 --> 39:54.800
must be a state

39:54.800 --> 39:55.500
that the exterior

39:55.500 --> 39:56.800
has actually finished

39:56.800 --> 39:57.540
delivering.

39:57.980 --> 39:59.060
And the paper proves

39:59.060 --> 39:59.640
that a system

39:59.640 --> 40:01.120
can satisfy the statistical

40:01.120 --> 40:02.000
screening condition

40:02.000 --> 40:03.040
perfectly on paper,

40:03.300 --> 40:04.600
but fail completely

40:04.600 --> 40:05.920
in physical reality

40:05.920 --> 40:06.920
because of the timing

40:06.920 --> 40:07.660
of the updates.

40:08.200 --> 40:09.140
Let's break down

40:09.140 --> 40:10.340
exactly why this happens.

40:11.200 --> 40:12.940
A stationary probability law,

40:13.540 --> 40:14.860
our screening condition,

40:15.380 --> 40:16.920
samples typical times.

40:17.720 --> 40:18.760
If you observe the system

40:18.760 --> 40:19.740
randomly over the course

40:19.740 --> 40:20.160
of a month,

40:20.300 --> 40:21.000
on average,

40:21.360 --> 40:22.200
the math holds up.

40:22.200 --> 40:24.160
But the internal system

40:24.160 --> 40:25.820
doesn't act on average.

40:26.180 --> 40:27.800
It acts at highly specific,

40:28.020 --> 40:28.340
discrete,

40:28.500 --> 40:29.620
instantaneous moments,

40:30.100 --> 40:31.160
the exact instant

40:31.160 --> 40:32.700
the boundary is consumed

40:32.700 --> 40:34.480
and an internal update triggers.

40:34.960 --> 40:36.280
This is called sampling

40:36.280 --> 40:37.720
typical events.

40:38.220 --> 40:38.360
Okay.

40:38.500 --> 40:39.760
I have an analogy for this

40:39.760 --> 40:40.460
to help separate

40:40.460 --> 40:41.340
typical times

40:41.340 --> 40:42.400
from typical events.

40:42.940 --> 40:44.780
Let's say our Markov blanket

40:44.780 --> 40:46.680
is a massive digital billboard

40:46.680 --> 40:47.300
in Times Square.

40:47.520 --> 40:47.680
Okay.

40:48.020 --> 40:49.320
The exterior environment

40:49.320 --> 40:51.120
is the complex computer server

40:51.120 --> 40:51.980
rendering the images.

40:51.980 --> 40:53.680
And the interior system

40:53.680 --> 40:54.760
is a person standing

40:54.760 --> 40:55.440
on the sidewalk

40:55.440 --> 40:56.660
looking up at the billboard

40:56.660 --> 40:57.660
to update their knowledge

40:57.660 --> 40:58.080
of the world.

40:58.260 --> 40:58.480
Makes sense.

40:58.960 --> 40:59.880
If you set up a camera

40:59.880 --> 41:00.660
to take a photograph

41:00.660 --> 41:01.440
of that billboard

41:01.440 --> 41:02.720
randomly every hour

41:02.720 --> 41:03.260
for a month

41:03.260 --> 41:04.640
and you run the statistics

41:04.640 --> 41:05.240
on those photos,

41:05.340 --> 41:06.440
you will find a perfect

41:06.440 --> 41:07.360
Markov blanket.

41:08.000 --> 41:09.460
The clean, rendered images

41:09.460 --> 41:10.340
displayed on the screen

41:10.340 --> 41:11.180
perfectly screen

41:11.180 --> 41:11.700
the pedestrian

41:11.700 --> 41:12.720
from the complex,

41:13.220 --> 41:14.300
messy, raw code

41:14.300 --> 41:15.300
running on the server.

41:15.800 --> 41:16.940
The screening condition

41:16.940 --> 41:17.960
holds flawlessly

41:17.960 --> 41:19.220
for typical times.

41:19.460 --> 41:20.940
That is the statistical average,

41:20.940 --> 41:22.400
but let's say

41:22.400 --> 41:23.140
this is a cheap

41:23.140 --> 41:24.180
laggy billboard.

41:24.180 --> 41:26.220
It takes three full seconds

41:26.220 --> 41:27.260
to render a new image.

41:27.960 --> 41:29.000
During those three seconds

41:29.000 --> 41:29.500
of rendering,

41:29.860 --> 41:30.540
it glitches out

41:30.540 --> 41:31.460
and actually flashes

41:31.460 --> 41:32.520
raw uncompiled

41:32.520 --> 41:33.660
HTML server code

41:33.660 --> 41:34.180
on the screen.

41:34.640 --> 41:35.940
The completion condition

41:35.940 --> 41:36.640
is violated

41:36.640 --> 41:37.720
because the data phase

41:37.720 --> 41:38.880
isn't fully ready.

41:39.400 --> 41:39.660
Uh-oh.

41:39.660 --> 41:42.200
Now, what if the pedestrian,

41:42.520 --> 41:43.440
the interior system,

41:43.840 --> 41:44.660
specifically chooses

41:44.660 --> 41:45.580
to look at the billboard

41:45.580 --> 41:46.860
only when it flickers

41:46.860 --> 41:47.340
and updates?

41:47.800 --> 41:48.460
They are sampling

41:48.460 --> 41:49.600
typical events.

41:50.000 --> 41:50.980
And in those specific

41:50.980 --> 41:51.480
instances,

41:51.760 --> 41:52.380
they are seeing

41:52.380 --> 41:53.060
the raw code.

41:53.200 --> 41:53.720
They are seeing

41:53.720 --> 41:55.100
the exterior environment

41:55.100 --> 41:55.680
directly.

41:56.040 --> 41:57.420
The blanket completely

41:57.420 --> 41:58.340
fails to screen them

41:58.340 --> 41:59.100
at the exact moment

41:59.100 --> 42:00.300
they actually update

42:00.300 --> 42:01.180
their internal state.

42:01.360 --> 42:02.660
That analogy captures

42:02.660 --> 42:03.660
the mathematical failure

42:03.660 --> 42:04.220
perfectly.

42:04.820 --> 42:06.060
The statistical blanket

42:06.060 --> 42:07.600
exists on average

42:07.600 --> 42:08.380
across time,

42:08.540 --> 42:10.340
but it fails in physical practice

42:10.340 --> 42:11.800
because the interior

42:11.800 --> 42:12.880
acts on stale,

42:13.080 --> 42:13.400
partial,

42:13.620 --> 42:14.620
or glitching data

42:14.620 --> 42:15.760
at the exact,

42:16.040 --> 42:16.740
critical moment

42:16.740 --> 42:17.560
of the update event.

42:18.420 --> 42:19.220
If the timing

42:19.220 --> 42:20.020
of the update event

42:20.020 --> 42:20.960
depends on both

42:20.960 --> 42:22.600
the inside and the outside

42:22.600 --> 42:23.060
jointly,

42:23.440 --> 42:24.120
like the pedestrian

42:24.120 --> 42:24.760
looking only

42:24.760 --> 42:25.720
when the screen glitches,

42:26.220 --> 42:27.260
the screening fails

42:27.260 --> 42:28.780
precisely when it matters most.

42:29.360 --> 42:30.980
So average doesn't cut it.

42:31.220 --> 42:31.600
Exactly.

42:32.080 --> 42:33.040
You have to evaluate

42:33.040 --> 42:34.300
the statistical condition

42:34.300 --> 42:36.060
not just vaguely over time,

42:36.400 --> 42:37.340
but specifically

42:37.340 --> 42:39.060
at the exact instance

42:39.060 --> 42:40.140
the interface is actually

42:40.140 --> 42:41.280
consumed by the interior.

42:41.940 --> 42:42.240
Which means

42:42.240 --> 42:43.860
a theoretical biologist

42:43.860 --> 42:44.660
could point to

42:44.660 --> 42:45.900
a beautifully mathematical

42:45.900 --> 42:46.920
Markov blanket

42:46.920 --> 42:47.680
in a brain model,

42:47.800 --> 42:48.880
but that blanket

42:48.880 --> 42:50.020
might be functionally

42:50.020 --> 42:51.700
useless to the actual organism

42:51.700 --> 42:53.320
because its internal neurons

42:53.320 --> 42:54.520
are firing out of sync

42:54.520 --> 42:55.740
with the sensory inputs

42:55.740 --> 42:56.680
arriving at the boundary.

42:57.240 --> 42:57.800
Precisely.

42:58.400 --> 42:59.080
And this is why

42:59.080 --> 42:59.960
Flyxion proposes

42:59.960 --> 43:01.180
a new, combined,

43:01.700 --> 43:02.460
rigorous definition

43:02.460 --> 43:03.660
for biological models.

43:04.240 --> 43:05.120
For an interface

43:05.120 --> 43:06.400
to be truly adequate,

43:06.400 --> 43:07.500
must satisfy

43:07.500 --> 43:08.320
both conditions

43:08.320 --> 43:08.900
simultaneously.

43:09.960 --> 43:10.280
First,

43:10.380 --> 43:11.380
the statistical screening

43:11.380 --> 43:12.000
must hold

43:12.000 --> 43:12.920
under the specific

43:12.920 --> 43:13.960
probability law

43:13.960 --> 43:14.960
of the instance

43:14.960 --> 43:15.820
at which the blanket

43:15.820 --> 43:16.520
is consumed,

43:16.880 --> 43:17.720
not just on average.

43:18.500 --> 43:18.860
Second,

43:19.300 --> 43:19.980
every update

43:19.980 --> 43:20.640
of the interior

43:20.640 --> 43:21.840
must strictly act

43:21.840 --> 43:23.260
only on a blanket value

43:23.260 --> 43:24.040
that has fully

43:24.040 --> 43:25.700
chronologically reached

43:25.700 --> 43:26.480
the data phase.

43:27.160 --> 43:27.760
It has to be

43:27.760 --> 43:28.920
statistically independent

43:28.920 --> 43:31.160
and chronologically complete.

43:31.400 --> 43:31.660
Yes.

43:31.660 --> 43:33.640
And whether a biological

43:33.640 --> 43:34.300
interface,

43:34.540 --> 43:35.640
like an ion channel

43:35.640 --> 43:36.760
in a cellular membrane

43:36.760 --> 43:38.980
or synaptic transmission

43:38.980 --> 43:40.080
in a neural network,

43:40.260 --> 43:41.440
actually satisfies

43:41.440 --> 43:42.700
these two rigorous conditions

43:42.700 --> 43:43.860
is an empirical,

43:44.340 --> 43:44.840
testable,

43:45.280 --> 43:45.920
physical matter.

43:46.340 --> 43:46.980
It's not something

43:46.980 --> 43:48.100
you can just assume

43:48.100 --> 43:48.720
to be true

43:48.720 --> 43:49.540
simply because you

43:49.540 --> 43:51.100
drew a four-part graph

43:51.100 --> 43:51.760
on a whiteboard.

43:52.480 --> 43:53.240
We have torn down

43:53.240 --> 43:54.600
a staggering amount

43:54.600 --> 43:55.580
of assumptions today.

43:55.980 --> 43:56.980
We've seen how

43:56.980 --> 43:58.200
physical sparse coupling

43:58.200 --> 43:59.480
fails to create boundaries

43:59.480 --> 44:00.280
out of equilibrium,

44:01.000 --> 44:01.680
how the existence

44:01.680 --> 44:02.280
of boundaries

44:02.280 --> 44:03.460
is completely relative

44:03.460 --> 44:04.460
to the observer's

44:04.460 --> 44:05.340
choice of description,

44:06.000 --> 44:07.180
how biological survival

44:07.180 --> 44:08.360
metrics aren't inherent

44:08.360 --> 44:09.020
in the math,

44:09.540 --> 44:10.400
and how the asynchronous

44:10.400 --> 44:11.280
flow of time

44:11.280 --> 44:12.720
can shatter a statistical

44:12.720 --> 44:14.120
shield in an instant.

44:14.500 --> 44:15.460
We have dismantled

44:15.460 --> 44:16.120
the overreach.

44:16.760 --> 44:18.340
But to be rigorously

44:18.340 --> 44:19.260
fair to the mathematics,

44:19.660 --> 44:20.240
because the math

44:20.240 --> 44:21.340
itself is not wrong,

44:21.700 --> 44:22.540
only the biological

44:22.540 --> 44:23.840
interpretation of it is,

44:24.360 --> 44:25.240
we need to establish

44:25.240 --> 44:26.900
exactly what a Markov blanket

44:26.900 --> 44:28.640
does legitimately give us.

44:28.640 --> 44:29.820
This brings us

44:29.820 --> 44:31.080
to the final tally,

44:31.660 --> 44:32.240
what the blanket

44:32.240 --> 44:33.400
actually licenses

44:33.400 --> 44:34.800
and what it does not.

44:35.480 --> 44:35.880
Let's start

44:35.880 --> 44:36.440
with the positive.

44:37.160 --> 44:37.920
What does finding

44:37.920 --> 44:38.860
a Markov blanket

44:38.860 --> 44:40.480
mathematically license

44:40.480 --> 44:41.380
a scientist to say

44:41.380 --> 44:42.060
about a system?

44:42.540 --> 44:43.760
It licenses three

44:43.760 --> 44:44.620
very specific

44:44.620 --> 44:45.580
powerful claims.

44:46.020 --> 44:47.580
First, it licenses

44:47.580 --> 44:48.820
that under a given

44:48.820 --> 44:49.800
chosen description

44:49.800 --> 44:50.460
of variables

44:50.460 --> 44:51.700
and under a specific

44:51.700 --> 44:52.820
probability law,

44:53.320 --> 44:54.420
one block of variables

44:54.420 --> 44:55.760
is statistically screened

44:55.760 --> 44:56.900
from another by a third.

44:57.560 --> 44:57.780
Okay.

44:57.780 --> 44:59.420
Conditional independence

44:59.420 --> 45:00.720
definitively exists,

45:01.260 --> 45:02.120
but only within

45:02.120 --> 45:03.320
the subjective confines

45:03.320 --> 45:04.560
of the specific map

45:04.560 --> 45:06.000
the scientist chose to draw.

45:06.500 --> 45:07.500
What's number two?

45:07.960 --> 45:08.840
Number two involves

45:08.840 --> 45:09.400
an additional,

45:09.760 --> 45:10.460
highly technical,

45:10.640 --> 45:11.440
mathematical condition

45:11.440 --> 45:13.660
called the modal fiber condition.

45:14.460 --> 45:15.880
If this specific condition

45:15.880 --> 45:16.340
is met,

45:16.760 --> 45:17.760
the blanket licenses

45:17.760 --> 45:18.440
the construction

45:18.440 --> 45:20.320
of a synchronization map.

45:20.840 --> 45:22.000
Let's explain

45:22.000 --> 45:23.400
this synchronization map.

45:23.860 --> 45:24.880
The paper talks about

45:24.880 --> 45:27.320
mu bar and eta bar.

45:27.320 --> 45:28.520
which represent

45:28.520 --> 45:29.320
the most likely

45:29.320 --> 45:30.260
internal state

45:30.260 --> 45:31.100
and the most likely

45:31.100 --> 45:32.040
external state

45:32.040 --> 45:33.680
given a specific state

45:33.680 --> 45:34.300
of the blanket.

45:34.660 --> 45:34.940
Yes.

45:35.340 --> 45:37.360
If the external mode map

45:37.360 --> 45:38.300
is constant

45:38.300 --> 45:39.040
on the fibers

45:39.040 --> 45:40.460
of the internal mode map,

45:40.660 --> 45:41.400
which simply means

45:41.400 --> 45:42.580
if every time

45:42.580 --> 45:43.300
the internal state

45:43.300 --> 45:44.600
settles on a specific

45:44.600 --> 45:45.300
likely state,

45:45.760 --> 45:46.580
the external state

45:46.580 --> 45:47.600
also reliably,

45:48.080 --> 45:49.100
consistently settles

45:49.100 --> 45:50.740
on a corresponding

45:50.740 --> 45:51.560
likely state,

45:51.960 --> 45:53.320
then you can mathematically

45:53.320 --> 45:54.580
construct a set

45:54.580 --> 45:55.500
theoretic function

45:55.500 --> 45:57.080
that maps the inside

45:57.080 --> 45:57.920
to the outside.

45:58.340 --> 46:00.160
So the math proves

46:00.160 --> 46:01.500
that the inside state

46:01.500 --> 46:02.720
correlates predictably

46:02.720 --> 46:03.520
and reliably

46:03.520 --> 46:04.860
with the outside state?

46:05.000 --> 46:05.240
Yes.

46:06.240 --> 46:07.180
And thirdly,

46:07.560 --> 46:08.680
it licenses the use

46:08.680 --> 46:09.160
of the blanket

46:09.160 --> 46:10.180
as a sufficient,

46:10.620 --> 46:11.580
complete interface

46:11.580 --> 46:12.880
for statistical inference.

46:13.280 --> 46:14.320
If you are building

46:14.320 --> 46:15.640
an artificial intelligence

46:15.640 --> 46:17.220
or doing complex

46:17.220 --> 46:18.220
statistical modeling,

46:18.820 --> 46:19.620
finding the blanket

46:19.620 --> 46:21.420
guarantees you absolutely

46:21.420 --> 46:22.500
do not need to look

46:22.500 --> 46:23.180
beyond it

46:23.180 --> 46:24.160
to make the most

46:24.160 --> 46:25.040
accurate possible

46:25.040 --> 46:25.960
prediction about

46:25.960 --> 46:26.540
the interior.

46:27.260 --> 46:27.900
So it remains

46:27.900 --> 46:29.180
an incredibly powerful,

46:29.420 --> 46:30.320
indispensable tool

46:30.320 --> 46:31.080
for data science,

46:31.180 --> 46:32.400
AI, and statistical modeling.

46:32.800 --> 46:33.560
Absolutely powerful.

46:34.340 --> 46:36.160
But now we must firmly state

46:36.160 --> 46:37.480
what it does not license.

46:38.340 --> 46:40.060
The ultimate reality check.

46:40.280 --> 46:40.720
Hit us.

46:41.100 --> 46:41.500
First,

46:42.000 --> 46:43.100
it absolutely does not

46:43.100 --> 46:43.980
license the claim

46:43.980 --> 46:44.700
that the mathematical

46:44.700 --> 46:45.560
partition marks

46:45.560 --> 46:46.420
an objective,

46:47.020 --> 46:47.760
physical boundary

46:47.760 --> 46:48.840
in physical reality.

46:48.840 --> 46:50.180
As we saw

46:50.180 --> 46:50.820
with the graph paper,

46:51.120 --> 46:51.760
simply rotating

46:51.760 --> 46:52.580
the plane of measurement

46:52.580 --> 46:53.440
destroys the boundary.

46:54.080 --> 46:55.100
The physical boundary

46:55.100 --> 46:56.200
is entirely relative

46:56.200 --> 46:57.040
to the description

46:57.040 --> 46:58.080
chosen by the observer.

46:58.520 --> 46:59.060
What's the second?

46:59.600 --> 47:00.160
Second,

47:00.660 --> 47:01.460
it does not license

47:01.460 --> 47:01.800
the claim

47:01.800 --> 47:02.620
that the interior

47:02.620 --> 47:04.800
represents the exterior

47:04.800 --> 47:05.860
in any cognitive,

47:06.100 --> 47:06.520
psychological,

47:06.680 --> 47:07.700
or conscious sense.

47:08.260 --> 47:09.500
The synchronization map

47:09.500 --> 47:10.300
we just talked about,

47:10.860 --> 47:11.740
that's just a set

47:11.740 --> 47:12.500
theoretic function.

47:13.000 --> 47:13.740
You can find that

47:13.740 --> 47:14.820
exact same mathematical

47:14.820 --> 47:15.880
function in systems

47:15.880 --> 47:17.000
that are completely dead,

47:17.260 --> 47:18.100
like a thermostat

47:18.100 --> 47:19.100
or a rock rolling

47:19.100 --> 47:19.580
down a hill

47:19.580 --> 47:21.320
where no scientist

47:21.320 --> 47:22.240
would ever claim

47:22.240 --> 47:23.760
a mind or a conscious

47:23.760 --> 47:25.020
representation exists.

47:25.500 --> 47:26.280
So calling it a belief

47:26.280 --> 47:26.920
is a stretch.

47:27.300 --> 47:28.260
To say the internal state

47:28.260 --> 47:29.200
is a belief

47:29.200 --> 47:30.540
about the outside world

47:30.540 --> 47:32.260
is an interpretive,

47:32.440 --> 47:33.360
philosophical leap

47:33.360 --> 47:34.580
added on top of the math.

47:34.840 --> 47:36.300
The math does not supply

47:36.300 --> 47:37.560
the concept of a belief.

47:37.840 --> 47:38.520
And finally,

47:38.600 --> 47:39.060
the big one.

47:39.780 --> 47:40.220
Finally,

47:40.620 --> 47:41.580
it does not license

47:41.580 --> 47:42.100
the claim

47:42.100 --> 47:43.200
that a subject,

47:43.740 --> 47:44.380
a self,

47:44.380 --> 47:45.660
or a living individual

47:45.660 --> 47:46.280
is present.

47:47.280 --> 47:48.460
Finding a Markov blanket

47:48.460 --> 47:49.460
does not prove

47:49.460 --> 47:49.920
you have found

47:49.920 --> 47:50.780
a living organism.

47:51.740 --> 47:52.880
Individuation requires

47:52.880 --> 47:54.060
completely separate,

47:54.300 --> 47:55.980
additional biological criteria

47:55.980 --> 47:57.720
like the delegated viability

47:57.720 --> 47:58.340
we discussed

47:58.340 --> 48:00.320
that the pure statistical

48:00.320 --> 48:01.080
formalism

48:01.080 --> 48:02.680
simply does not contain.

48:03.220 --> 48:03.560
Together,

48:03.760 --> 48:04.800
this is the profound

48:04.800 --> 48:05.360
main thesis

48:05.360 --> 48:06.320
of Flyxion's paper.

48:06.740 --> 48:07.640
The Markov blanket

48:07.640 --> 48:09.560
is simply a closure condition

48:09.560 --> 48:10.200
on a description.

48:10.600 --> 48:11.340
It's a statement

48:11.340 --> 48:12.840
that for a given law

48:12.840 --> 48:14.100
in a chosen set of variables,

48:14.720 --> 48:15.820
the mathematical dependence

48:15.820 --> 48:16.720
between two blocks

48:16.720 --> 48:18.020
is mediated entirely

48:18.020 --> 48:18.640
by a third.

48:19.120 --> 48:20.220
It is a precise,

48:20.600 --> 48:21.960
beautiful statistical tool.

48:22.300 --> 48:23.360
But its physical,

48:23.660 --> 48:24.120
biological,

48:24.440 --> 48:25.100
and psychological

48:25.100 --> 48:25.900
interpretations

48:25.900 --> 48:27.360
depend on a mountain

48:27.360 --> 48:28.040
of assumptions

48:28.040 --> 48:29.520
that the formalism itself

48:29.520 --> 48:31.240
simply does not deliver.

48:31.480 --> 48:32.680
It is a perfect,

48:33.000 --> 48:33.880
cautionary example

48:33.880 --> 48:34.940
of how dangerous

48:34.940 --> 48:35.500
it can be

48:35.500 --> 48:36.860
when a highly specialized

48:36.860 --> 48:37.840
mathematical tool

48:37.840 --> 48:38.740
from one field,

48:39.280 --> 48:39.800
in this case,

48:40.020 --> 48:41.060
AI and statistics,

48:41.060 --> 48:42.360
is imported

48:42.360 --> 48:43.480
into another field

48:43.480 --> 48:44.580
and asked to carry

48:44.580 --> 48:45.620
the weight of massive

48:45.620 --> 48:46.760
philosophical questions

48:46.760 --> 48:47.900
it was never designed

48:47.900 --> 48:48.340
to answer.

48:49.080 --> 48:49.560
The literature

48:49.560 --> 48:50.680
has been most productive

48:50.680 --> 48:52.660
when it is explicitly clear

48:52.660 --> 48:53.720
about all the additional

48:53.720 --> 48:54.880
biological conditions

48:54.880 --> 48:55.700
it is asserting.

48:56.200 --> 48:56.980
But when it claims

48:56.980 --> 48:57.700
the math alone

48:57.700 --> 48:58.680
proves the biology,

48:59.340 --> 49:00.260
the logic collapses.

49:00.800 --> 49:01.240
Listener,

49:01.340 --> 49:02.260
I want to sincerely

49:02.260 --> 49:02.800
thank you

49:02.800 --> 49:03.460
for taking this

49:03.460 --> 49:04.460
incredibly dense,

49:04.600 --> 49:05.740
immensely rewarding

49:05.740 --> 49:06.940
deep dive with us today

49:06.940 --> 49:08.220
into the mathematics

49:08.220 --> 49:09.520
of boundaries.

49:10.100 --> 49:10.720
We went from

49:10.720 --> 49:12.100
the digital weather station

49:12.100 --> 49:12.700
on your wall

49:12.700 --> 49:14.220
through the swirling currents

49:14.220 --> 49:16.040
of out-of-equilibrium systems,

49:16.700 --> 49:17.520
tilted the axes

49:17.520 --> 49:18.380
of reality,

49:18.880 --> 49:19.940
and ended up staring

49:19.940 --> 49:20.740
at the glitching

49:20.740 --> 49:21.700
digital billboards

49:21.700 --> 49:23.060
of asynchronous computing.

49:23.560 --> 49:24.760
We tore down the myth

49:24.760 --> 49:26.140
that math automatically

49:26.140 --> 49:27.040
proves the existence

49:27.040 --> 49:28.180
of your physical self

49:28.180 --> 49:29.740
and revealed the beautiful

49:29.740 --> 49:31.060
subjective complexity

49:31.060 --> 49:32.100
of how we choose

49:32.100 --> 49:33.020
to describe the world.

49:33.020 --> 49:34.880
It is a vital reminder

49:34.880 --> 49:35.940
that science requires

49:35.940 --> 49:37.020
rigorous precision

49:37.020 --> 49:37.900
not just in our

49:37.900 --> 49:38.860
mathematical equations

49:38.860 --> 49:40.920
but in how we philosophically

49:40.920 --> 49:42.300
interpret those equations.

49:42.780 --> 49:43.840
And as we wrap up,

49:43.920 --> 49:44.540
I want to leave you

49:44.540 --> 49:45.240
with a final,

49:45.580 --> 49:46.400
provocative thought

49:46.400 --> 49:46.960
to mull over,

49:47.400 --> 49:48.160
something that builds

49:48.160 --> 49:48.780
on everything

49:48.780 --> 49:49.700
we've discussed today.

49:50.220 --> 49:51.480
We've firmly established

49:51.480 --> 49:52.640
that Markov blankets

49:52.640 --> 49:54.260
are just closure conditions

49:54.260 --> 49:55.640
based on our chosen descriptions.

49:56.180 --> 49:57.140
They depend entirely

49:57.140 --> 49:58.000
on the variables

49:58.000 --> 49:59.320
we decide to group together

49:59.320 --> 50:00.340
and the scale

50:00.340 --> 50:01.540
at which we choose to look.

50:01.720 --> 50:01.940
Right.

50:01.940 --> 50:03.440
But what happens

50:03.440 --> 50:05.280
when an artificial intelligence

50:05.280 --> 50:06.680
programmed with the very

50:06.680 --> 50:07.700
mathematical principles

50:07.700 --> 50:09.040
of active inference

50:09.040 --> 50:10.580
begins to rewrite

50:10.580 --> 50:12.240
its own Markov blankets?

50:12.860 --> 50:14.200
If an AI can mathematically

50:14.200 --> 50:15.160
redraw its own

50:15.160 --> 50:16.160
statistical boundaries

50:16.160 --> 50:17.340
by simply changing

50:17.340 --> 50:18.640
its internal description

50:18.640 --> 50:19.180
of the world,

50:19.640 --> 50:20.180
coarse graining

50:20.180 --> 50:21.300
its variables here,

50:21.700 --> 50:22.800
rotating its coordinate

50:22.800 --> 50:23.620
planes there,

50:24.240 --> 50:26.240
where does its self end

50:26.240 --> 50:28.020
and its environment begin?

50:28.540 --> 50:29.660
We might be on the verge

50:29.660 --> 50:31.380
of building non-biological minds

50:31.380 --> 50:32.700
whose very physical

50:32.700 --> 50:33.780
and cognitive boundaries

50:33.780 --> 50:34.600
are nothing more

50:34.600 --> 50:36.220
than a matter of real-time

50:36.220 --> 50:37.560
mathematical choice.

50:38.100 --> 50:38.660
If the boundary

50:38.660 --> 50:39.560
is just a description,

50:40.400 --> 50:41.360
what happens when the machine

50:41.360 --> 50:42.660
learns to rewrite the description?

50:43.300 --> 50:44.900
That is a staggering implication.

50:45.360 --> 50:47.100
The map literally redesigning

50:47.100 --> 50:48.960
the territory in real time.

50:48.960 --> 50:51.240
So the next time you look at a map

50:51.240 --> 50:52.600
or try to draw a line

50:52.600 --> 50:53.740
in the sand between yourself

50:53.740 --> 50:54.820
and the rest of the universe,

50:55.000 --> 50:55.460
just remember,

50:55.820 --> 50:56.860
you might feel like

50:56.860 --> 50:57.480
you're pointing out

50:57.480 --> 50:58.380
an undeniable

50:58.380 --> 50:59.600
objective absolute,

50:59.820 --> 51:00.540
but you're really just

51:00.540 --> 51:01.600
picking the description

51:01.600 --> 51:02.720
that makes the most sense

51:02.720 --> 51:03.860
to you right now.

51:04.460 --> 51:06.380
The sand is always moving.

51:07.160 --> 51:08.580
The boundaries are yours to draw.

51:09.440 --> 51:10.640
Keep questioning the edges

51:10.640 --> 51:11.620
of your own world.

51:12.400 --> 51:13.440
Catch you on the next Deep Dive.

